So it's always useful
and quite fascinating

00:42:36.510 --> 00:42:39.090
to hear about real
implementations from customers.

00:42:39.090 --> 00:42:40.940
And I guess one thing
I want to highlight,

00:42:40.940 --> 00:42:42.180
which was particularly
fascinating,

00:42:42.180 --> 00:42:44.263
was the fact that they
built one complex use case,

00:42:44.263 --> 00:42:45.960
and then they found
out, oh, guess what?

00:42:45.960 --> 00:42:47.850
I can take what
I've implemented,

00:42:47.850 --> 00:42:51.010
and with small tweaks,
convert it into a new use.

00:42:51.010 --> 00:42:52.860
So that was quite fascinating.

00:42:52.860 --> 00:42:57.310
And the tools on GCP
do enable that easily.

